/// Chapter 32 of the guide, written from md-docs/reference/project-structure.md by
/// scripts/docsite/guide.py; edit the guide, not this file.
page ProjectGuide(path: "/reference/project", title: "Project structure", description: "Where files go, how they merge into one program, naming in a global namespace, wf generate, what to commit, and how to grow a project.", layout: DocsShell("Project structure", chapter: t("nav.group.ship"), blurb: "Where files go, how the compiler reads them, how names work across a project, and how a project grows without getting lost.", source: "md-docs/reference/project-structure.md", sections: [Anchor(id: "the-layout", label: "The layout"), Anchor(id: "one-program-with-no-imports", label: "One program, with no imports"), Anchor(id: "names-across-a-project", label: "Names across a project"), Anchor(id: "files-that-are-not-wf", label: "Files that are not .wf"), Anchor(id: "generate-a-starter-file", label: "Generate a starter file"), Anchor(id: "choose-what-to-commit", label: "Choose what to commit"), Anchor(id: "organise-a-growing-project", label: "Organise a growing project"), Anchor(id: "quick-reference", label: "Quick reference")], prevTo: "/docs/guide/performance", prevLabel: t("ch.31"), nextTo: "/docs/guide/static-and-spa", nextLabel: t("ch.33"))) {
    Stack(gap: .lg) {
        Markdown("A WebFluent project is a config file and a folder of sources that the compiler reads as one program. The folders are a convention for you and your team; the compiler does not care where a declaration lives. This chapter explains how a project is laid out and read, then shows you how to add files, choose what to commit and keep a growing project in order.\n\nIn this chapter:\n\n- the conventional layout, and which files are required;\n- how the compiler merges every file into one program, and what that means for names;\n- what happens to the files that are not `.wf`;\n- how to generate starter files, what to commit, and how to organise a project as it grows.")

        Heading("The layout", id: "the-layout").h2

        Markdown("This is the layout `wf init` starts from, with every kind of file a project can hold:")

        CodeBlock(#"my-site/
├── AGENTS.md               the language reference, for a coding agent (`wf init` writes it)
├── webfluent.app.json      the config (see Configuration)
├── .env                    build-time values, not committed (see Environments)
├── src/
│   ├── App.wf              the app shell and the Router
│   ├── theme.wf            themes
│   ├── types.wf            shared types, enums, constants, data
│   ├── api.wf              services
│   ├── pages/              one page per file
│   ├── components/         components
│   ├── stores/             stores
│   ├── styles.css          your own stylesheets, anywhere under src/
│   ├── tilt.js             your own scripts, anywhere under src/
│   ├── translations/       en.json, ar.json (with "i18n" in the config)
│   ├── posts.json          data files a `data` declaration reads
│   └── about.md            Markdown pages
├── public/                 copied to the build's root: favicon, fonts, images
├── tests/                  `test` declarations, and __snapshots__/
└── build/                  what `wf build` writes (not committed)"#, title: "text")

        Markdown("Only two things are required: `webfluent.app.json` and one `.wf` or `.wfx` file under `src/`. Everything else is convention. The config is covered in [Configuration](/reference/config), and `.env` in [Environments](/docs/guide/environments).")

        Heading("One program, with no imports", id: "one-program-with-no-imports").h2

        Markdown("The compiler reads every `.wf` and `.wfx` file under `src/` and merges them into a single program. A page uses a component declared in another file, and a component uses a store, by name. There is nothing to import.\n\nFor example, a component declared in `src/components/PriceCard.wf` and a page in `src/pages/Pricing.wf` work together with no import between them. Here they are in one block:")

        CodeBlock(#"// In src/components/PriceCard.wf
component PriceCard(_ plan: String, price: Number) {
    Card {
        Text(plan).bold
        Text(format(price, .currency))
    }
}

// In src/pages/Pricing.wf
page Pricing(path: "/pricing", title: "Pricing", description: "Plans and prices.") {
    Heading("Pricing").h1
    PriceCard("Team", price: 49)
}"#, title: "wf")

        Markdown("The compiler reads `App.wf` (or `App.wfx`) first, then the rest in path order. The order matters for nothing but the order of equal things in the output.\n\n`use Store` at the top of a page or component says that it reads that store. It documents the dependency for the reader and the editor; it does not scope anything, and a page reads a store by name with or without it.")

        Heading("Names across a project", id: "names-across-a-project").h2

        Markdown("Because every file is one program, the namespace is global. Two components, two pages, two stores, two types or two constants with one name is an `E102` error, naming both places.\n\nThe conventions that keep names apart:\n\n- **Declared names are PascalCase**: pages, components, stores, types, enums, themes, services and animations.\n- **Constants are UPPER_SNAKE** by convention: `API`, `PAGE_SIZE`.\n- **A page's name is its identity, not its title.** Add a suffix when the name would collide with a component: `page PostPage` beside `component Post`.\n- **A component that one page uses** can live in that page's file.")

        Heading("Files that are not .wf", id: "files-that-are-not-wf").h2

        Markdown("The build reads other files too. What each becomes:")

        Table(caption: "Files that are not .wf") {
            Table.Head {
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell("File").header
                    Table.Cell("Where").header
                    Table.Cell("Becomes").header
                }
            }
            Table.Body {
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`*.css`") }
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("anywhere under `src/`") }
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("bundled into `styles.css`, in path order, after the built-ins' rules") }
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`*.js`") }
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("anywhere under `src/`") }
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("copied to `js/` as written and linked on every page before the compiled code; its top-level names are in scope ([JavaScript interop](/docs/guide/interop))") }
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`*.md`") }
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("under `src/`") }
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("a page ([Content](/docs/guide/content#write-a-page-as-a-md-file))") }
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`*.json`") }
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("named by a `data` declaration") }
                    Table.Cell("a constant, read at build time")
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell("images")
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("named by an `image` declaration") }
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("resized, hashed files and a `<picture>` ([Media](/docs/guide/media))") }
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`translations/*.json`") }
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("the `i18n.dir`") }
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("the locale tables ([Internationalization](/docs/guide/i18n))") }
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell("anything")
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`public/`") }
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("copied as it is to the build's root: `public/favicon.svg` is `/favicon.svg`") }
                }
            }
        }

        Heading("Generate a starter file", id: "generate-a-starter-file").h2

        Markdown("To add a page, a component or a store with the boilerplate written for you, run `wf generate`:")

        Terminal(lines: [
                Line(command: "wf generate page Pricing"),
                Line(command: "wf generate component PriceCard"),
                Line(command: "wf generate store Cart")
            ])

        Markdown("Each command writes a starter declaration in the conventional folder:")

        Table(caption: "Generate a starter file") {
            Table.Head {
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell("Command").header
                    Table.Cell("Writes").header
                }
            }
            Table.Body {
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`wf generate page Pricing`") }
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`src/pages/Pricing.wf`, with `path: \"/pricing\"`, a title, a description and an `h1`") }
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`wf generate component PriceCard`") }
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`src/components/PriceCard.wf`") }
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`wf generate store Cart`") }
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`src/stores/cart.wf`") }
                }
            }
        }

        Markdown("In a project written in `.wfx`, the files are `.wfx`. `wf generate` never overwrites a file: when one exists, it says so and stops. Add `-d DIR` to generate into a project other than the current directory.")

        Heading("Choose what to commit", id: "choose-what-to-commit").h2

        Markdown("Commit the sources and the config:\n\n- `webfluent.app.json`\n- `src/`\n- `public/`\n- `tests/`, with its `__snapshots__/`\n\nLeave out what the build writes and what is private. Add these lines to `.gitignore`:")

        CodeBlock(#"build/
.wf-cache/
.wf-sizes.json
.env"#, title: "text")

        Markdown("`.wf-cache/` holds resized images between builds. `.wf-sizes.json` records what the last build weighed, for `wf build --stats` to compare against. `.env` holds build-time values that may be private.")

        Heading("Organise a growing project", id: "organise-a-growing-project").h2

        Markdown("As a project grows, these habits keep it readable:\n\n- **Group by feature once folders get long.** A `src/billing/` folder that holds the billing pages, components, store and types reads better than four folders that each hold a slice of it. The compiler does not mind either way.\n- **Put each service in one place.** Write one `api` per backend, in its own file, with the types its endpoints return beside it.\n- **Keep shared types together**, in a `types.wf` per area, so the editor's go-to-definition lands somewhere predictable.\n- **Document as you declare.** A `///` comment above a component, a prop, an event or a type shows on hover and in `wf docs`, the gallery of everything the project declares.\n- **Hold every file to the formatter.** `wf fmt --check` in CI keeps every file in one layout ([Testing](/docs/guide/testing#run-the-checks-in-ci)).")

        Heading("Quick reference", id: "quick-reference").h2

        Table(caption: "Quick reference") {
            Table.Head {
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell("Topic").header
                    Table.Cell("Rule").header
                }
            }
            Table.Body {
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell("Required files")
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`webfluent.app.json` and one `.wf` or `.wfx` file under `src/`") }
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell("Reading order")
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`App.wf` first, then the rest in path order") }
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell("Imports")
                    Table.Cell("none: every declaration is in scope by name")
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`use Store`") }
                    Table.Cell("documents a dependency; scopes nothing")
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell("Duplicate names")
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`E102`, naming both places") }
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`public/`") }
                    Table.Cell("copied to the build's root as it is")
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell("Starter files")
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`wf generate page`, `component` or `store`, then the name") }
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell("Not committed")
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`build/`, `.wf-cache/`, `.wf-sizes.json`, `.env`") }
                }
            }
        }
    }
}
